From fbf99f7c8581169378fb13685562e166acb03b60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:21:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] library: a double-quoted Windows path may end in a
 backslash (#2685)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed
- words() let a backslash escape the closing double quote, so a path
  typed "C:\Program Files\" — the trailing separator a folder leaves —
  kept the quote open and the rest of the line folded into one word:
  the review of 4e4191e1 asked for a decision and a test. Inside quotes
  a backslash is now a byte, the way cmd and PowerShell take it, and
  only a quote closes a quote; nothing this field carries needs a
  literal " inside a double-quoted word. Outside quotes nothing moves:
  my\ server is still one word with a space.

Run
- the new cases in library-mcp-windows-command.test.cjs — a double-
  quoted path ending in a backslash, saved, then the server reopened
  and saved again — red on 4e4191e1 under chromium, en and zh (the
  quote never closed: command "C:\Program Files\" -y pkg saved as one
  word), green after on chromium and webkit, en and zh, as are
  library-mcp-copy-config and library-servers-bulk, and
  mcp-editor-cancel alone (its busy-machine reds of the 4e4191e1 round
  didn't come back).
- the red on 4e4191e1 is the ablation too: branch client.js, new test
  kept.
- node --check client.js clean.

